      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "model/Independent post-settlement sponsor payout in NftWon allows a malicious or transfer-restricted prizeToken to strand winner redemption after sponsor collects 95% of USDC proceeds",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "The clean design specification states both that 'arbitrary prize contracts and ticket recipients are untrusted' and that 'Settlement is permissionless, storage-only; redemption requires current ticket owner, burns claim atomically, and must revert all effects on delivery failure. Sponsor and treasury can claim independently after settlement.' In the implementation, RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams and RaffleFactory.createRaffle only verify that prizeToken has deployed code, is not a known protocol address, supports IERC721 via ERC-165, and transfers ownership of prizeTokenId to the clone at creation. Once a raffle resolves to Status.NftWon, _settleWinningTicket allocates 95% of unsettledPot to sponsorProceeds and 5% to protocolFees without transferring or testing delivery of the prize NFT. Because releaseSponsorProceeds does not require prizeClaimed or winnerRedeemed to be true, a sponsor who supplies an untrusted prizeToken (or a prizeToken that becomes paused, blacklisted, or reverts on outbound transferFrom/ownerOf after initial escrow) can settle and withdraw 95% of the canonical USDC proceeds while redeemWinningTicket permanently reverts for the winning ticket owner, with no fallback transition to Status.Refunding. (Note: IRaffle.sol lines 14-15 narrow the code's trust assumption in NatSpec to 'honest, standards-compliant ERC-721s', which diverges from the specification's untrusted prize contract assumption.) Defensive property for owner review: for any raffle resolved to Status.NftWon under an untrusted prizeToken model, either sponsor proceeds release should be conditioned on successful prize delivery (prizeClaimed == true) or a bounded recovery/refund path should exist if prizeToken delivery fails.\nAssumptions: The stated design requirement that arbitrary prize contracts are untrusted applies, rather than the narrower IRaffle NatSpec assumption that supported prizes are honest, standards-compliant ERC-721s.; The configured prizeToken succeeds during initial safeTransferFrom escrow in createRaffle but subsequently reverts or fails to update ownerOf during outbound transferFrom in redeemWinningTicket (due to malicious logic, pause, freeze, or transfer restrictions)."
          },
