        {
          "ruleId": "model/Pre-deployment CREATE addresses of future Raffle clones bypass _isProtocolDestination screening until those clones are created",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "RaffleFactory.createRaffle deploys clones via Clones.clone(raffleImplementation), which uses the CREATE opcode whose target address is deterministically derived from the factory address and nonce. Raffle._isProtocolDestination screens out known protocol plumbing and queries canonicalFactory.isRaffle(destination) only when destination.code.length != 0. Before a future raffle clone is deployed, its predicted CREATE address has code.length == 0 and isRaffle == false, so it is accepted as protocolTreasury (in RaffleFactory.constructor), as sponsorRecipient (in RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams and Raffle.initialize), or as a ticket recipient (in Raffle._update via buyEntries or transferFrom). Once RaffleFactory later deploys a clone at that nonce-derived address and sets isRaffle[raffle] = true, _isProtocolDestination returns true for that address, causing _transferQuote to revert with InvalidQuoteDestination and stranding any quote-token claims or tickets assigned to that address. Defensive property for owner review: no address that can ever become isRaffle[addr] == true should hold tickets or be configured as a payout recipient, or recipient screening should be invariant across the lifetime of the factory.\nAssumptions: A caller or deployer intentionally or accidentally supplies a precomputed future CREATE address of RaffleFactory as protocolTreasury, sponsorRecipient, or a ticket recipient before that clone is created, and the factory subsequently reaches that nonce."
          },
