        {
          "ruleId": "model/Prize NFT release in redeemWinningTicket and releaseSponsorPrize uses raw transferFrom without ERC-721 receiver checks",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "During raffle creation, RaffleFactory.createRaffle escrows the prize using prize.safeTransferFrom, and Raffle.buyEntries mints tickets using _safeMint. However, when the prize NFT is released to the winner in Raffle.redeemWinningTicket or returned to sponsorRecipient in Raffle.releaseSponsorPrize, the contract calls prizeToken.transferFrom(address(this), recipient, prizeTokenId) followed by an ownerOf check rather than safeTransferFrom. While using transferFrom avoids onERC721Received callback reentrancy or revert griefing (particularly during permissionless releaseSponsorPrize), RaffleFactory._validateCreateParams does not verify that a contract sponsorRecipient supports IERC721Receiver, and a winning ticket may have been transferred via ERC721.transferFrom to a contract that does not implement IERC721Receiver or relies on onERC721Received hooks to record incoming NFTs. Defensive property for owner review: any contract configured as sponsorRecipient or redeeming a winning ticket must be able to custody and transfer the prizeToken NFT without relying on an onERC721Received callback.\nAssumptions: sponsorRecipient (or a contract winner that acquired the winning ticket via transferFrom) is a smart contract that can call redeemWinningTicket or receive the prize via releaseSponsorPrize but cannot manage ERC-721 tokens delivered without an onERC721Received callback."
          },
